- Line 152 - idempotency marker off by one. Exact input: `check_text("# lint:known-mispairing\nNCT01453608 EFFECT-HF", vocab, own_of, vocab_re, True)` with `vocab={"CONFIRM-HF":{"NCT01453608"},"EFFECT-HF":{"NCT03037931"}}` and matching `own_of`. Consequence: a documented “just above” exemption does not exempt, while the same marker one line below wrongly suppresses the defect.

- Line 231 - positive-control can report wrapper success without proving the control fired. Exact input: run `--positive-control` with a non-empty cache containing only `{"protocolSection":{"identificationModule":{"acronym":"ABCD","nctId":"NCT00000000"}}}`. Consequence: the command exits `0` with zero hits even though the promised known mispairings were not detected.

- Lines 115 and 218-219 - instrument scans a different corpus than it reports. Exact input: add `tests/bad.py` containing `NCT01453608 EFFECT-HF` with the vocab above, then run the script. Consequence: files outside `root/ssot/scripts/docs` are scanned while the report says only those scan roots were used.

- Lines 46-47 - instrument reads a different copy by default. Exact input: `RM_CTGOV_CACHE` unset, current repo cache contains `NCT01453608 -> CONFIRM-HF`, but the hardcoded temp cache lacks that record. Consequence: the current worktree can pass because validation used a stale unrelated cache.

- Line 49 - selector is not keyed to an exact NCT token. Exact input: `check_text("XNCT01453608 EFFECT-HF", vocab, own_of, vocab_re, False)` with the vocab above. Consequence: a substring inside a non-ID token is treated as a real registration id.

